From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lycaos <caraboune@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:36:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] prompts-modal: /prompts browser for system and subagent
 templates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Catalogue, TUI editing, presets under ~/.grok, user docs and changelog.

Carried into the patch queue so it survives upstream syncs. It was written
directly on the 1.0.0 sync branch with no Gork-Patch-Id trailer, so it was
never exported to maint/patches — and `patchctl apply` rebuilds the branch
from upstream plus the queue alone. The 1.0.1 repatch dropped it silently.

Marked critical for the same reason: a trailing non-critical patch is
skipped on conflict, which would repeat that silent loss. A conflict here
must stop the sync and be ported by hand.

Ported to 1.0.3 with two conflicts, both trivial: `prompt/mod.rs` (upstream
added `browser_verification` next to this patch's `catalog`; both kept) and
the shell CHANGELOG (the Unreleased section now sits above 1.0.1-1.0.3).

Presets became per session in 1.0.16. A preset directory is the source of
truth instead of a shared working copy, each session binds to one by id in
`prompt-presets/.state.json`, and `PromptContext` carries the session id so
resolution stays correct in a leader process hosting several sessions at
once. The old shape mirrored every edit into the active preset and let
`apply` rewrite one shared `prompts/` directory, so two sessions could not
hold two prompt sets and an experiment silently rewrote the preset it
started from.

Saving onto a name that exists now asks instead of overwriting (the
`PresetExists` error was declared and never constructed), `c` no longer
deletes anything — it points the session at the built-in defaults — and the
modal gains rename, duplicate, a filter over the preset list, per-preset
metadata and a permanent source indicator. `/prompts` takes list/use/save/
update/defaults so presets are drivable without the modal. Pre-existing
overrides are promoted once into a preset, non-destructively.

Gork-Patch-Id: prompts-modal
Gork-Risk: low
